    "longest_thought": "Landorus-Therian is at 44% HP and poisoned, so it will die from poison in a few turns. Garchomp has Earthquake which hits Landorus-Therian super effectively (Ground vs Ground/Flying = 2x), but Garchomp is only at 24% HP and would likely be KO'd by one more Earthquake. Toxapex at 49% HP can take a neutral Earthquake hit and survive, then Toxic Spikes or Recover to stall out the poison. Dondozo at 100% HP with Body Press (Fighting) is neutral to Landorus-Therian but has great bulk. Gholdengo at 100% HP could use Nasty Plot + Shadow Ball, but its Thunderbolt is useless against a Flying-type.\n\nThe deciding factor: I need something that can survive an Earthquake hit and either KO or stall out the poisoned Landorus-Therian. Dondozo at full HP with Body Press (Fighting, neutral) can take the hit and chip away, while Toxapex can set up Toxic Spikes for future threats. But Garchomp's Earthquake would likely 2HKO Landorus-Therian if it survives one turn...\n\nActually, let me reconsider: Garchomp at 24% HP (86/357) taking a neutral Earthquake from Landorus-Therian (ATK ~145 base, probably boosted). That would likely KO Garchomp. So switching to Garchomp is risky.\n\nToxapex at 49% can survive one Earthquake and then Recover or Toxic Spikes. But it's already been hit by Earthquakes multiple times.\n\nDondozo at 100% HP with Body Press (Fighting, neutral) - this is the safest option. It can take a full Earthquake and still be functional. Body Press ignores Speed so it doesn't matter that Landorus-Therian is faster.\n\nActually wait - I should think about what wins. Landorus-Therian is poisoned at 44%. If I switch in something that survives, the poison will kill it in ~7 more turns. But I also want to pressure it. Dondozo with Body Press (Fighting, neutral) at full HP can take a hit and deal decent damage. Garchomp's Earthquake would be ideal but too fragile.\n\nI'll go with Dondozo - full HP, can survive the Earthquake, and Body Press deals solid neutral damage while Landorus-Therian slowly dies from poison.",
